INT. PLANETARIUM DOME - AFTER HOURS

The false sky hangs overhead, a hush of ten thousand painted stars. Reclined seats form concentric rings below. The projector at the centre hums like a sleeping animal.

IMOGEN VASSEUR, thirties, in a green coat, sits in the third row with her shoes off, one foot tucked beneath her. Beside her, TAVIAN OKONJO, thirties, tie loosened, holds a paper bag of roasted chestnuts, steam curling from the top.

TAVIAN
Orion.

IMOGEN
That's Cassiopeia.

TAVIAN
It has a belt.

IMOGEN
It has a W.

They laugh and reach into the bag at the same moment. Their hands collide inside it. They both freeze, fingers touching chestnut shells, the heat of the paper between them. Neither pulls away.

Overhead, the sky rotates one degree. A meteor streaks across the dome, projected, perfect.

IMOGEN (CONT'D)
(softly)
Tavian. I got the fellowship.

His fingers loosen. The bag tilts. Chestnuts roll out across the seat and fall one by one into the dark. He does not catch them.

TAVIAN
Where?

IMOGEN
Santiago.

They both look up at a sky that suddenly seems very large.
